  "related_material": "ca_perovskite_tetragonal",
  "notes": "The separate ca_perovskite_tetragonal card represents the I4/mcm model used by later studies. Chen et al. (2018), DOI 10.2138/am-2018-6087, p. 465, favors octahedral rotation but leaves the exact space group uncertain. Sun et al. (2022), DOI 10.2138/am-2021-7913, p. 113, identifies a 211 reflection favoring I4/mcm among the four tested tetragonal models. Those later observations do not uniquely determine the structure of the Shim (2002) samples, whose pseudocubic c/a is less than one."
